WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.750
Manaus, Brazil.

2
00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:07.090
Every month, the mean temperature
is 27 to 28 degrees Celsius.

3
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:08.650
Darwin, Australia.

4
00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:15.090
Every month, the mean maximum is
between 30.7 and 33.4 degrees Celsius.

5
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:18.290
Around Manaus: dense rainforest.

6
00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:20.550
Around Darwin: savanna.

7
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.330
Is Darwin just hotter?

8
00:00:22.380 --> 00:00:24.170
Does it get far less rain?

9
00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.670
So why is one city ringed by
rainforest, and the other by savanna?

10
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.930
In this mission, you'll read
climate graphs for both cities,

11
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:35.510
and follow water into and out of the soil.

12
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.050
Then you'll see how plants and
animals in each biome respond,

13
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.750
from the canopy to herds on the move.

14
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.770
Your mission: explain why Manaus
is surrounded by rainforest,

15
00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.390
but Darwin by savanna.
